# Audit-only SwiftLint config (SwiftLint's own defaults, used to find complexity
# hotspots the project config's raised thresholds hide). Not part of any build.

# Rendered icon previews — regenerate with `python3 scripts/generate-icon.py --preview`.
# The SVG sources next to them ARE tracked; these are just for eyeballing.
design/*.png
design/icon-candidates/*.png

# Demo-video sources. The raw per-segment takes (183 MB of 4K screen recording) and
# the 12 MB master export are both reproducible — the takes by re-running
# ./scripts/record-demo.sh, the master by re-exporting the ChatCut project named in
# notes/plans/20260816-candela-domain-site-v2.md. What the site actually serves is
# the small web encodes beside them, and those ARE tracked, because site/build.py
# copies them into docs/ and `build.py --check` fails if they are missing.
assets/footage/
assets/video/candela-hero-60s.mp4
